---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { ORG } from '../lib/seo';
import Navigation from '../components/Navigation.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import SEOHead from '../components/SEOHead.astro';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <SEOHead
    slot="head"
    title="About Bravo Zulu: How We Research Naval History"
    description="Bravo Zulu publishes sourced naval history stories about the world's warships. How we research and fact-check, how to send corrections, and who is behind the site."
  />
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "AboutPage",
    "url": "https://brvzulu.com/about/",
    "mainEntity": ORG
  })} />

  <Navigation active="about" showThemeToggle />

  <main id="main" class="about-page">
    <h1>About Bravo Zulu</h1>
    <p>
      Bravo Zulu is a research project dedicated to the history of the world's warships.
      We publish daily stories and in-depth articles covering everything from Civil War
      commerce raiders to Cold War nuclear tests.
    </p>
    <p>
      The name comes from the NATO signal flag code "BZ" — meaning "well done."
      It's the highest compliment one ship can signal to another.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each story starts with one fact that makes you stop and read the rest.
      Swipe through them on the <a href="/">Daily feed</a>, then read the full articles
      when one grabs you.
    </p>

    <h2>How we research a story</h2>
    <p>
      Every story starts from the record: ship logs, action reports, court-martial and inquiry
      transcripts, survivor memoirs, and the collections of naval history archives and museums such as
      the US Naval History and Heritage Command and the Imperial War Museums. We check names, ranks,
      dates, tonnage and casualty figures against at least two independent sources, and where sources
      disagree we say so in the text.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every article ends with the sources we used, linked where they are online, so you can check our
      work and keep reading.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If you spot an error, email <a href="mailto:stories@bravozulu.co">stories@bravozulu.co</a> with
      the story and a source. We fix confirmed errors in the article itself.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is behind Bravo Zulu</h2>
    <p>
      Bravo Zulu is published by <a href="https://mozuma.co" rel="noopener">MOZUMA</a>, a Cyprus-based
      studio that makes naval history graphic novels and collectibles, including
      <em>Come On, Texas</em>, a graphic novel about the battleship USS Texas. The stories on this site
      are free to read and always will be.
    </p>

    <h2>Tell us a story</h2>
    <p>
      Did someone in your family serve on a ship we should write about?
      <a href="/submit/">Send us their story</a>. Or browse the archive
      <a href="/topics/">by war, navy and theme</a>.
    </p>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + var(--banner-offset) + 3rem);
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    padding-right: 1.25rem;
  }

  .about-page h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-page h2 {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .about-page p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .about-page a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .about-social {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .about-social a {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .about-social a:hover {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
</style>
